{
 "about": "The pencil's grain tile (docs/dev/handwriting.md 'Client', 'Server'). frontend/src/ink/grain.js grainUri and gamma/ink.py grain_png write the same PNG for a colour, byte for byte: GRAIN_PX pixels square (the tile spans GRAIN_UNITS page units), a 2-bit palette image from a fixed seed (mulberry32 0x5eed1e55; white noise over a smooth 4 px value noise, 0.7 / 0.3, cut at the 0.3, 0.45 and 0.7 quantiles into indices 0..3), its palette the colour four times with tRNS alphas 0, 128, 204 and 255, IDAT one stored zlib block. Only the colour varies: #rrggbb, #rgb or rgb[a](r, g, b[, a]) after trimming JavaScript's whitespace, each channel Number() rounded half up and clamped to 0..255 (a NaN writes 0), the alpha left out, black for anything else. `png` is the file as base64; the SVG export fills a pencil with it in a <pattern> anchored at the page's corner and the PDF writers with a tiling pattern of the same tile.",
